# 19. Concurrency

Since we decided earlier to use:

```text
httpx.AsyncClient
async/await
```

we can run permitted connectors concurrently:

```text
                 SearchManager
                      |
        +-------------+-------------+
        |             |             |
        v             v             v
    RemoteOK       Wellfound       YC
        |             |             |
        +-------------+-------------+
                      |
              +-------+-------+
              |       |       |
              v       v       v
            Indeed Naukri Foundit
```

That means we don't wait:

```text
RemoteOK → finish
then Wellfound
then YC
then Naukri
```

Instead:

```text
RemoteOK ──────┐
Wellfound ─────┤
YC ────────────┤
Indeed ────────┤
Naukri ────────┤
Foundit ───────┤
Hirist ────────┤
Cutshort ──────┤
Freshersworld ─┘
       ↓
   AGGREGATE
```

subject to each source's permitted access/rate limits.

---

# 20. We should also add source health monitoring

Because some sites will fail.

For every connector:

```text
source
last_success
last_failure
jobs_found
jobs_saved
duplicates
blocked
response_time
error
```

Example:

```text
RemoteOK
Status: SUCCESS
Jobs: 42

Wellfound
Status: SUCCESS
Jobs: 18

Naukri
Status: BLOCKED
Action: Disabled

Hirist
Status: ACCESS_RESTRICTED
Action: Use permitted integration/public route
```

This is much better than allowing one blocked website to crash the entire agent.

Hirist, for example, explicitly says it uses technology to exclude robots and prohibits bypassing those controls. ([Hirist][2])

