# 22. Most important change to our Day 6 work

Our Day 6 shouldn't simply be:

```text
RemoteOK → SearchManager
```

It should be:

```text
                 SEARCH MANAGER
                       |
                 REGISTRY
                       |
          +------------+------------+
          |            |            |
       Remote        India       Recruiter
       Sources       Sources       Sources
          |            |            |
          +------------+------------+
                       |
                       v
                 JOB NORMALIZER
```

Then we add connectors one at a time.

---

# 23. One more thing: "all jobs in the world"

We should aim for **maximum practical coverage**, but I don't want to promise literally every job on the internet.

There are millions of company career pages and many private/restricted systems.

The better architecture is:

```text
Major Job Boards
+
Remote Job Sources
+
ATS Platforms
+
Company Career Pages
+
Authorized Recruiter Sources
+
Permitted Public Sources
```

This can give the agent **very broad coverage** without relying on prohibited scraping.

Indeed, for example, provides an official developer/integration framework with restrictions on how its APIs and data may be used, so we should use official/approved access where available rather than attempting to bypass controls. ([Indeed Documentation][3])

---

## Final target for your project

Your agent should ultimately behave like this:

```text
                 YOUR RESUME
                     |
                     v
              CAREER PROFILE
                     |
                     v
             SEARCH CONFIGURATION
                     |
                     v
       +-------------+-------------+
       |             |             |
       v             v             v
   REMOTE JOBS   INDIA JOBS   RECRUITER POSTS
       |             |             |
       +-------------+-------------+
                     |
                     v
                TODAY ONLY
                     |
                     v
             FULL JD / POST
                     |
                     v
             EXPERIENCE 0–2
                     |
                     v
               ROLE MATCH
                     |
                     v
               SKILL MATCH
                     |
                     v
                SCORE 0–100
                     |
                     v
               QUALIFIED JOB
                     |
            +--------+---------+
            |                  |
            v                  v
       APPLY LINK         REAL EMAIL
            |                  |
            |             TAILORED RESUME
            |                  |
            |             PERSONALIZED EMAIL
            |                  |
            +--------+---------+
                     |
                     v
              APPLICATION LOG
                     |
                     v
              EXCEL REPORT
                     |
                     v
                EMAIL REPORT
                     |
                     v
               EVERY 6 HOURS
```

**So yes: keep RemoteOK, Wellfound, Y Combinator and all the connectors we have already planned, and expand the connector registry to cover the Indian portals and recruiter-post sources.** The key is that each connector only handles **source acquisition**; the filtering, experience detection, resume matching, tailoring, application and reporting should be centralized so every source follows exactly the same rules.

And for LinkedIn specifically, we should not build a login/scraping/bypass mechanism. LinkedIn's current rules prohibit unauthorized scraping and unauthorized automated access; its crawling terms say automated crawling requires express permission. ([linkedin.com][4])

